
---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Mohtashim Ul Haq"
  description="Professional background, software engineering interests, and postgraduate study in Data Science at Universiti Sains Malaysia."
>
  <article class="container section about-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Software engineering with a systems perspective.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I work on software development across application architecture,
        APIs, integrations, and deployment. My current project,
        IronForge, brings these disciplines together in an agentic
        SaaS engineering environment.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Professional focus</h2>
      <p>
        My engineering interests include maintainable .NET applications,
        distributed application boundaries, AI-enabled workflows,
        tool integrations, and reliable software delivery.
      </p>
      <p>
        I value practical implementation: defining component
        responsibilities, documenting trade-offs, validating behavior,
        and making software reproducible to build and deploy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <article class="card education-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Postgraduate study · In progress</p>
        <h3>Master's in Data Science</h3>
        <p class="institution">Universiti Sains Malaysia (USM)</p>
        <p>
          My postgraduate study complements my software engineering
          work by developing my understanding of data-driven methods
          and their application in software systems.
        </p>
        <p class="small-note">
          Academic research topics and completed coursework will be
          added as they are confirmed and can be documented accurately.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Current engineering project</h2>
      <h3>IronForge</h3>
      <p>
        IronForge is my flagship project for exploring end-to-end
        software engineering across Blazor, ASP.NET Core APIs, MCP
        integration, internal agent workflows, MAUI Blazor Hybrid,
        PostgreSQL, Docker, and cloud deployment.
      </p>
      <a href="/projects/ironforge/">Explore the IronForge case study →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Areas of interest</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Reliable, maintainable .NET application architecture.</li>
        <li>Agentic systems and tool-based integrations.</li>
        <li>API design, authorization, and integration boundaries.</li>
        <li>Cross-platform application development.</li>
        <li>Cloud deployment, testing, and operational reliability.</li>
        <li>Practical applications of data science and machine learning.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Résumé</h2>
      <p>
        For a concise overview of my professional experience,
        technical skills, and education, see my résumé.
      </p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/documents/resume.pdf" download>
        Download résumé (PDF)
      </a>
      <p class="small-note">
        The PDF must be added to the public/documents directory before
        this download link is published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        For software engineering opportunities or project enquiries,
        use the contact page.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact me</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .page-intro {
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 740px;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .about-section {
    padding-block: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .education-card {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .education-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .institution {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .small-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
